{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00643",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.4,
      "end_seconds": 15.39,
      "duration_seconds": 13.99,
      "text": "Right, I'm here for the hand. They said to come back, but I've got to be somewhere by two, so can we crack on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.25,
      "end_seconds": 27.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "We'll be as quick as safely possible. Remind me what happened, I've only got the triage note. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.62,
      "end_seconds": 42.11,
      "duration_seconds": 12.49,
      "text": "Chopping onions. The knife slipped, cut across the palm, on the left. It bled like mad. I had it glued and strapped up yesterday at the walk-in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.53,
      "end_seconds": 51.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "Okay. Did anything else happen, did you feel your fingers go numb?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.66,
      "end_seconds": 57.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "No. No numbness, fingers all move."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.17,
      "end_seconds": 65.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "And has it been oozing at all, or leaking through the dressing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.06,
      "end_seconds": 70.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "No. Dry as a bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.19,
      "end_seconds": 77.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, or felt feverish?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.48,
      "end_seconds": 82.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "No. Not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 84.29,
      "end_seconds": 91.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "I've got the dressing trolley, doctor, shall I take the old one off? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.39,
      "end_seconds": 103.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "Please, Kerry. Mr Barlow, this will be easier if we take the dressing off together, if that's all right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.8,
      "end_seconds": 107.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Go on. Quickly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 124.93,
      "end_seconds": 127.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Sorry, that'll sting a little."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.17,
      "end_seconds": 140.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Thanks. That's looking tidy. The edges are together, there's no redness around it and no pus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.8,
      "end_seconds": 144.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "So it's healing? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.13,
      "end_seconds": 155.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "It's healing well. While we're here, I'll update your record. Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.89,
      "end_seconds": 159.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "None."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.08,
      "end_seconds": 165.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.93,
      "end_seconds": 174.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Just ibuprofen, 400 mg, when it throbs. Not often."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.04,
      "end_seconds": 180.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Good. And your health background?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.2,
      "end_seconds": 190.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, and asthma, though I haven't needed the inhaler in years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 193.03,
      "end_seconds": 197.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Do you want the glue left on, doctor? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.71,
      "end_seconds": 209.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "Yes, it'll come off by itself in a week or so. Kerry, use a clean dry dressing over the top. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 211.22,
      "end_seconds": 213.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Of course. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.06,
      "end_seconds": 220.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Mr Barlow, any operations on this hand before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.72,
      "end_seconds": 230.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "Carpal tunnel on that wrist, in 2020. This scar here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.1,
      "end_seconds": 246.78,
      "duration_seconds": 14.68,
      "text": "I see it. Thank you. It's good that the glued wound is clean. With diabetes I want to be extra careful, so keep it dry for the next five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.38,
      "end_seconds": 252.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Can I wash up? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.14,
      "end_seconds": 263.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Wear a rubber glove over a dry dressing, or let someone else do it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 266.26,
      "end_seconds": 271.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "I'll give you spare dressings to take with you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.74,
      "end_seconds": 275.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Thanks. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 277.05,
      "end_seconds": 281.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Change it every day, and keep it clean."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.86,
      "end_seconds": 295.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.7,
      "text": "And if it gets red, swollen, starts to ooze, or you get a temperature, come straight back or go to the urgent care centre."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.72,
      "end_seconds": 300.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Right. Will do. Can I go now? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.33,
      "end_seconds": 305.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "You can. Mind that hand. ~"
    }
  ]
}
